# Classified Stage 3 differences (scripts/tcc-matrix.py): CASE<TAB>DIVERGES|DEFECT<TAB>CLASS<TAB>REASON.
# CLASS: compiler limitation | linker limitation | ABSD ABI defect | kit divergence. Each case is pinned
# in <case>.txt (stdout, --, stderr, --, status) and must equal its pin and differ from the Linux reference.
alloc	DIVERGES	kit divergence	NATIVE LIMIT (kit contract 2, 3; Stage 1 divergences.txt `alloc`): the 32 MiB heap window ends the churn loop with ENOMEM near 31 MiB live and refuses 40 MiB malloc and realloc (original kept); Linux allocates all of it. Byte-equal to the kit's own Stage 1 pin c/tests/kit/shell-expected/alloc.txt
errno	DIVERGES	kit divergence	DELIBERATE INCOMPATIBILITY (kit contract 5, 6; Stage 1 divergences.txt `errno`): /bin and /etc are read-only mounts of the session, so create in /bin and write-open of /etc are EROFS where Linux (no root) says EACCES, and ENOENT on a host without /etc/motd; the cwd-relative O_CREAT|O_EXCL lines and the rest agree
exit.abort	DIVERGES	kit divergence	DELIBERATE INCOMPATIBILITY (kit contract 2; Stage 1 FAULTS `exit abort`): ABSD has no signals, abort() ends the process with status 134 (128 + SIGABRT; the kernel's USER EXIT status=134) where Linux reports SIGABRT (-6); stdout (ctor, main, abort, flushed first) equals gcc's Linux build
stack.frame1m	DIVERGES	compiler limitation	tcc emits no stack probes (tcc x86_64-gen.c:1596-1599, the ELF prologue's bare `sub $v,%rsp`; `__chkstk` only under TCC_TARGET_PE, :1019-1022; kit docs/C-INTERFACE.md:571-572 makes stack-clash probes part of the contract for frames crossing the guard): frame1m's prologue moves RSP down 1 MiB at once and its first store (sum, about 1 MiB below the frame base) is far below the mapped stack; the ABSD stack grows one page directly below the mapped range with RSP in or above that page (kernel process.rs stack_growth_page; kit contract A4, which the kit's clang build meets with -fstack-clash-protection), so the store faults (USER FAULT vector 14) and the shell reports `ended abnormally`, 128, before anything is printed; Linux grows its stack for any access and prints frame1m sum=21
stack.overflow	DIVERGES	kit divergence	DELIBERATE INCOMPATIBILITY (kit contract 2; Stage 1 FAULTS `stack overflow`): the recursion reaches the end of the 4 MiB stack and faults (USER FAULT vector 14); ABSD has no signals, the shell reports `ended abnormally`, 128, where Linux reports SIGSEGV (-11); stdout (about to overflow, flushed first) equals Linux
